998 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 515 0 R
/E (Under normal conditions, the electron is a subatomic particle classified as a fermion, which means it has a half-integral spin \(a quantum mechanical property of particles where their intrinsic angular momentum is a half-integer multiple of the reduced Planck constant\), obeying the Pauli Exclusion Principle \(no two electrons can have the same four electronic quantum numbers, meaning they cannot exist at the same place at the same time\), but once 2 electrons form a pair their spins align in the opposite direction to one another, resulting in the net spin of 0.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
