1035 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 518 0 R
/E (In countries like Japan and Germany, superconducting magnets are used in experimental magnetic levitation \(maglev\) trains, allowing them to hover above the tracks and therefore minimise friction, improving efficiency and speed. Similarly, superconducting magnets play a crucial role in particle accelerators, where they are used to guide and focus particle beams for the study of fundamental atomic and subatomic structures.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1036 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 518 0 R
/E (Later another breakthrough in physics occurred - the discovery of the cuprate high temperature superconductors \(HTS\) in 1986, which gave a new momentum to the field and intensified the research towards the development of superconductors that can operate at even higher, potentially room, temperatures, which continues to this day.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1037 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 518 0 R
/E (IV. Real life applications of superconductors)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1038 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 518 0 R
/E (Superconductors already have a range of practical applications, as cooling materials to the boiling points of liquid helium or hydrogen is technically feasible. However, conditions of their use are quite demanding in the face of high costs and complicated logistics used to maintain sufficient temperatures. )
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
1039 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 518 0 R
/E (Superconducting materials have been explored for use in high-speed connections between components inside high-level computer chips, where reduced electrical resistance can significantly improve performance. In medicine, superconducting coils enabled the generation of extremely strong magnetic fields in devices such as magnetic resonance imaging \(MRI\) scanners, which are used to produce detailed images of soft tissues within the human body, improving treatments that involve precise surgeries like brain tumor removal. )
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
