1063 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 519 0 R
/E (Today people hardly imagine life without electronic devices such as mobile phones and computers. One of their important uses is to make distant communication possible. Signals sent by the devices to a certain address travel through the air in high-frequency wave form and through wires as electrical signals. In highly dense settlements hundreds of thousands of users use their devices simultaneously to exchange messages with each other within the small volume of air relative to the number of the users, hence there will arise invisible traffic jams in the air. Modern technology enables billions of devices to share the same space to transmit data simultaneously without having a large signal interference. The aim of the article is to give readers a general view of what the wireless communication system is like.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
1064 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 519 0 R
/E (Regulations of invisible Traffic Jams)
/Pg 27 0 R
