1066 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 519 0 R
/E (Analogue signals, the data pieces in different forms \(e.g., electrical signal, audio, etc.\), are converted into digits of 0s and 1s [3]. A transmitter \(the apparatus that generates radio waves, modulates their amplitude or frequency, and transmits them by means of an antenna [1]\) of the phone turns the digits to an electromagnetic wave of a certain frequency [2]. The wave travels to the nearest base station. The base station transmits the data to the Mobile Telephone Switching Office \(MTSO\) in the same form. Each call provider company owns one MTSO. )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [16 2434 0 R 18 2435 0 R 20 2436 0 R 22]
>>
