<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 520 0 R
/E (TDMA divides transmission of the same frequency into frames, and each frame is further divided into time slots \(e.g., a 10 ms time frame taken on a specific wave frequency is divided for 5 users chronologically, leaving each user with a time slot of 2 ms\). Each user transmits during their allocated time slot, and only one user transmits at a time. This technique works well with slow voice data signals and is useful for compressed video and other high-speed data [10].)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [25 2440 0 R 27]
>>
