/P 521 0 R
/E (Now returning to CDMA, the spreading code increases the bandwidth of the signal, allowing it to spread over a wide frequency band. The assigned code to the user, consisting of 1s and 0s, is attached to the original data when transmitted. At the receiver end, the signal is demodulated using the same code to extract the original information. For example, using 64 unique codes allows up to 64 users to occupy the same frequency channel at the same time without interfering with each other. CDMA is used in GPS \(Global Positioning System\) and in 3G mobile networks [6].)
/Pg 29 0 R
