/S /P
/P 521 0 R
/E (Another advanced access technique is Orthogonal Frequency Division Multiple Access, or OFDMA, which is used in Long-Term Evolution, LTE, systems to accommodate multiple users in a given bandwidth. OFDMA is a modulation method that divides a channel into multiple narrow orthogonal \(it means unrelated, not affected by one another\) bands that are spaced so they overlap but do not interfere with each other. Every band is divided into hundreds or even thousands of 15-kHz-wide subcarriers. The data to be transmitted is divided into many lower-speed bit streams and modulated onto the subcarriers. Time slots within each subcarrier are used to package the data to be transmitted. This allows for high data rates and reduces interference [6].)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [10 2443 0 R 12]
>>
endobj
