1151 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 523 0 R
/E (One of the most promising renewable energy sources is photovoltaic \(PV\)/solar generators. These systems convert sunlight directly into electricity using the photovoltaic effect, in which photons strike a semiconductor material \(usually silicon\) and release electrons from its atoms. These electrons are then pushed in one direction, due to a built-in electric field, generating an electric current. This technology is an excellent alternative to traditional fossil fuels or crude oil due to its clean nature and scalability. However, these systems do have their limitations. Their output relies solely on sunlight availability \(solar irradiation\), which varies with time of day, weather conditions, and seasonal changes.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
