<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 524 0 R
/E (Fuel cells are another highly efficient and sustainable energy technology. These systems use an electrochemical reaction, through which they generate electricity. Most commonly, this reaction happens between hydrogen and oxygen, without the need for combustion. Inside this cell, hydrogen molecules are split into protons and electrons at the anode.  These protons then pass through an electrolyte membrane, forcing the electrons to travel through an external circuit, thus creating an electric current.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
