1171 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 525 0 R
/E (At the cathode, protons and electrons recombine with oxygen to form water, making water the by-product of this process. Fuel cells are a very attractive alternative to fossil fuels, offering clean energy generation with high efficiency and minimal emissions. However, their widespread use faces challenges, including high production costs and durability issues. Despite these limitations, the integration of fuel cells into hybrid energy systems holds great potential as a clean energy source and as an output regulator, given their nature [8], as shown in Fig. 4. )
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1172 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 525 0 R
/E (Figure 3: Schematic diagram of a hydroelectric generator and turbine, rendered via generative AI [24].)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
1173 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 525 0 R
/E (Hybrid renewable energy systems \(HRES\) are integrated power generation systems that combine two or more energy sources, such as solar, wind, hydro, biomass, fuel cells, and even conventional non-renewable sources such as diesel or natural gas, into a single interconnected system. The purpose of these systems is to solve the above-mentioned issues and increase efficiency as well as reliability. For example, solar power is abundant during the daytime but unavailable at night. At the same time, wind generation can be stronger during evenings or seasonal changes that dampen solar irradiation, allowing one source to balance and fill in the shortcomings of the other. These systems usually incorporate batteries or hydrogen systems to ensure a continuous energy output and address intermittency. By addressing the intermittency issues of standalone renewable systems, these setups help minimise energy shortages and reduce dependence on fossil fuels. They can be implemented in both grid-connected and off-grid applications, making them suitable for both urban and rural areas. Overall, hybrid renewable energy systems present a practical solution to achieving cleaner, more resilient, and more efficient energy production, while aligning with global sustainability goals. For these reasons, an analysis of different hybrid renewable energy systems is presented [9].)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
1174 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 525 0 R
/E (Figure 4: Schematic illustration of a proton exchange membrane fuel cell, rendered via generative AI [25])
/Pg 33 0 R
