/P 525 0 R
/E (III. Literature Review, Modelling, Utilisation, and Analysis of Hybrid Renewable Energy Systems)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
1177 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 525 0 R
/E (An integration scheme has been proposed for a wind and solar hybrid energy system that uses both the rotor and grid converters of a Doubly Fed Induction Generator \(DFIG\) to transfer power from the photovoltaic array to the electrical grid [10]. In this configuration, the DFIG typically used in wind turbines serves as a central interface for managing and optimising the flow of energy from different sources. By channelling photovoltaic-generated electricity through the existing DFIG converters, the system effectively minimises the need for additional hardware, reduces conversion losses, and simplifies overall design. )
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
