/P 527 0 R
/E (Currently, a significant portion of total energy consumption in most countries goes to space heating and cooling, as well as hot water usage [12]. To reduce the use of fossil fuels as energy generators as well as their impact on the environment, the use of widely available renewable energy systems, such as solar, should be considered for the specific use of space heating and hot water usage. However, the issue of solar irradiance fluctuation has been raised, and the combination of solar energy generators with other renewable energy systems, such as biomass for regions rich in both resources or geothermal for regions with geothermal activity as well as solar irradiance, has been proposed [13], [14]. )
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [5]
>>
