/E (Tests, simulations, and prototypes showed that this setup keeps voltage steady, shares the load smoothly between sources, and does so with relatively low cost and simple hardware.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
1200 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 527 0 R
/E (Distributed generation is an increasingly popular concept in modern power systems. The purpose of such systems is to produce electricity at or near the point of consumption rather than relying solely on large, centralised power plants. This approach utilises both renewable and non-renewable sources, as well as storage technologies, to meet demand. On the non-renewable side, distributed generation systems usually consist of small combustion turbines or gas turbines, which can quickly provide power but still have issues of emissions and fuel dependency.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
1201 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 527 0 R
/E (18)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
