>>
endobj
1210 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 528 0 R
/E (To verify performance, simulations were run under normal conditions as well as under power disturbance scenarios to see how this microgrid would respond. The results show that these models behave in a realistic way and are feasible, and do not show obvious instability or failure, even though the paper does not emphasise strict performance metrics like efficiency or cost in detail.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
1211 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 528 0 R
/E (Ahmad et al. [21] present an experimental evaluation of a small-scale hybrid renewable system composed of a photovoltaic array and a wind turbine installed at the Lebanese University in Tripoli. The system, consisting of three PV panels and a 1 kW wind turbine connected to a battery bank and an inverter, was monitored from 2011 to 2015. The data was collected and analysed to determine the energy contribution of each source individually, as well as the combined performance of the hybrid setup.  Results show clear seasonal variations in output, with PV generation dominating during summer months while wind energy is more significant in other periods of the year. Over the five-year measurement period, annual production was estimated at 163.78 kWh for PV and 130.89 kWh for wind. )
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
1212 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 528 0 R
/E (19)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
