/E (Besides responding rapidly to an invading pathogen, our organism uses an immunological tolerance system. It is a state of unresponsiveness to self-antigens, which helps prevent the immune system from attacking healthy tissue. To put it another way, self-reactive \(able to trigger an autoimmune response\) T- and B-lymphocytes are destroyed at the maturation sites, suppressed by regulatory T-cells \(Treg\), or subjected to apoptosis \(cell death\). Failure to eliminate such cells may lead to the onset of autoimmune disea)
/Pg 43 0 R
