1342 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 538 0 R
/E (Ocular immune privilege represents a multilayered system of protection encompassing physical blood-ocular barriers, the production of anti-inflammatory cells, and peripheral immune tolerance. Together, these mechanisms minimise the risks of permanent loss of function and protect irreplaceable tissues from damage. In contrast to the old concepts, modern understanding of this process underpins the dynamic nature involving active interactions of immune cells and the specialised intraocular environment as opposed to passive isolation of eye tissues. )
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1343 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 538 0 R
/E (VI. Conclusion)
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1344 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 538 0 R
/E (Disruption of the ocular immune privilege following penetrating injury, surgical interventions or infections results in the exposure of sequestered antigens to the immune system, leading to the development of autoimmune disease. Sympathetic ophthalmia, as a primary example of this process, demonstrates the close relationship between immune tolerance breakdown and cell-mediated autoimmune response.)
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1345 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 538 0 R
/E (Further investigation into ocular immune privilege is of fundamental and clinical importance. Understanding deep molecular processes of local immune regulation may allow for alternative, more effective ways of treating or preventing autoimmune diseases, presenting us with innovative strategies for improving the success of corneal transplantations and tailoring treatments for inflammatory disorders of the eyes.)
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
1346 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 538 0 R
/E (The research in this field has largely advanced the current understanding of mechanisms underlying sympathetic ophthalmia as well as sophisticated the general concept of immune-privileged sites, contributing to the development of modern immunosuppressive therapeutic strategies.)
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
