/P 543 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 51 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
1456 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 543 0 R
/E (According to the United Nations, drug-resistant pathogens claim almost 1.3 million deaths each year and contribute to the deaths of nearly five million others. A more recent estimate published in The Lancet \(2024\) suggests that more than 39 million people will die from antibiotic-resistant infections between now and 2050.)
/Pg 51 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
1457 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 543 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 51 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
1458 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 543 0 R
/E (AMR is not only a clinical problem but also a multidimensional crisis that threatens global public health, requiring urgent attention from leaders across the security, healthcare and economic arenas. It is driven by the indiscriminate and excessive use of antibiotics, underscoring the critical importance of thorough antimicrobial stewardship and reinforced infection control interventions.)
/Pg 51 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
1459 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 543 0 R
/E (Furthermore, developing new antibiotics and investigating alternative treatments can provide sustainable solutions, but effective progress requires multidisciplinary approaches and stronger international co-operation.)
/Pg 51 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
