/P 545 0 R
/E ( I. Introduction: A Quiet Town, a Global Laboratory)
/Pg 53 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
1503 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 545 0 R
/E (The story of Pfizer Sandwich is, at its core, a story about what happens when sustained institutional investment meets scientific curiosity. It is also, inescapably, a story about Kent: about the infrastructure, talent, and geography that made a small English town the unlikely birthplace of blockbuster medicines. For students of chemistry, the site offers something rarer still, a case study in how fundamental concepts from the textbook, enzyme inhibition, structure activity relationships, and pharmacokinetics become medicines in the clinic.)
/Pg 53 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
1504 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 545 0 R
/E (Figure 1. The Pfizer research campus viewed from the banks of the River Stour, Sandwich, Kent. For over five decades, this site on the outskirts of a mediaeval Cinque Port served as the European research headquarters of one of the world's largest pharmaceutical companies, producing seven major medicines including fluconazole and sildenafil. The campus has since been redeveloped as Discovery Park. Image: Nick Smith / Geograph, CC BY-SA 2.0.)
/Pg 53 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
1505 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 545 0 R
/E (Figure 2. The Barbican, a mediaeval gatehouse on the River Stour in Sandwich, Kent. Sandwich's heritage as a Cinque Port town dates to the eleventh century, but it was the establishment of Pfizer's research campus on the town's outskirts in 1954 that transformed this quiet corner of East Kent into an unlikely centre of global pharmaceutical innovation. Image: Nilfanion / Wikimedia Commons, CC BY-SA 3.0.)
/Pg 53 0 R
/K [14]
>>
