/E (Figure 5. Structure of sildenafil \(UK-92,480\), a pyrazolopyrimidinone PDE5 inhibitor discovered at Pfizer Sandwich. The fused pyrazolopyrimidinone core \(blue\) binds selectively to the active site of PDE5. The compound was originally synthesised as a potential treatment for angina but was repositioned for erectile dysfunction after unexpected clinical observations during Phase I trials. Sildenafil was approved by the FDA on 27 March 1998 as the first oral treatment for erectile dysfunction. Diagram: K.S. Ye Yint, CATS Insights, 2026.)
