1582 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 551 0 R
/E (Figure 6. Buildings on the former Pfizer west site, now part of Discovery Park, Sandwich, Kent. Since Pfizer's withdrawal in 2011, the campus has been redeveloped as one of the United Kingdom's leading science and innovation hubs, hosting over 180 companies and more than 3,000 people across life sciences, biotechnology, and technology. Image: David Anstiss / Geograph, CC BY-SA 2.0.)
/Pg 59 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
1583 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 551 0 R
/E (The Pfizer Sandwich story offers several insights that extend beyond its specific institutional history. First, it demonstrates the relationship between sustained research investment and transformative outcomes: the fluconazole programme ran for over a decade from inception to clinical launch, and the sildenafil journey from cardiovascular hypothesis to erectile dysfunction approval spanned nearly as long. Breakthrough medicines are not produced quickly.)
/Pg 59 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
1584 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 551 0 R
/E (Second, the sildenafil case illustrates the importance of serendipity and scientific alertness. The compound's unexpected side effect in clinical trials could have been dismissed as a curiosity. Instead, the research team recognised its therapeutic potential, connected it to emerging basic science, and executed a successful repositioning. )
/Pg 59 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
1585 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 551 0 R
/E (41)
/Pg 59 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
