/E (Pure calcite is transparent. A single crystal of Iceland spar, the optically clear variety prized since the seventeenth century for its extraordinary birefringence, transmits light from approximately 250 nm to 2,500 nm with minimal absorption.7 So why are the Dover cliffs white?)
/Pg 62 0 R
/K [9]
