<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 554 0 R
/E (There is a practical corollary to these optics. The softness of chalk \(Mohs hardness 3, inherited directly from calcite\) means that the cliff face is continually being refreshed by coastal erosion. Wave undercutting at the base causes blocks of chalk to collapse, exposing fresh, unweathered surfaces. It is this constant renewal that keeps the cliffs white; a stable, unrefreshed chalk surface would gradually discolour as biological growth and atmospheric deposition accumulated.1 )
/Pg 62 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
