1729 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 559 0 R
/E ( This article traces that chemistry from alpha-acid isomerisation to terpene volatility and from mediaeval brewing to modern antimicrobial research. The hop, it turns out, is a chemistry lesson hiding in a pint glass.)
/Pg 67 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
1730 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 559 0 R
/E (Figure 1. Traditional oast houses on the Kent landscape near Bishopsbourne, Canterbury. The conical kilns were designed to channel heated air through freshly picked hops, reducing their moisture content from approximately 80% to 6% before packing. Image: Oast House Archive / Geograph, CC BY-SA 2.0.)
/Pg 67 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
