1820 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 566 0 R
/E (The difference in the empathetic display of male and female parents have resulted in conceived notions that mothers are more appropriate caretakers due to their higher capacity for empathy. This article explores the validity of this assumption through the insight of research providing insight into the difference in types and capacity for empathy in both sexes, along with its role in parenting and childhood development. It was suggested that the sex of the parent had little impact on the empathetic development of the child, rather the presence of responsive parenting was the determinate factor in the development of empathy in male and females.)
/Pg 74 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1821 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 566 0 R
/E (Abstract:)
/Pg 74 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1822 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 566 0 R
/E (Empathy: Impact of genetical factors in contrast with parenting by either sex)
/Pg 74 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1823 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 566 0 R
/E (Author: Minh Ngoc Nguyen)
/Pg 74 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
1824 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 566 0 R
/E (With the rise in single parent households of either sex, one may raise the question of whether one parent is more adequate for child-rearing than the other, as many continue to hold the belief that mothers are more suitable than fathers due to their supposed ability to be more empathetic. However, the validity of this assumption is debated greatly, due to it being based heavily on societal expectations and role enforcement. This leads to the question: Is empathy, although inherently learnt, influenced primarily by the sex of the parent or more dependent on innate, biological factors?)
/Pg 74 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
1825 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 566 0 R
/E (II. Concept of empathy)
/Pg 74 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
1826 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 566 0 R
/E ( Empathy is the idea of sympathising with and understanding the thoughts and emotions of someone else; it is primarily conceptualised into 2 types: Cognitive empathy and emotional empathy \(this essay will not discuss concepts of affective, compassionate and somatic empathy\).)
/Pg 74 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
1827 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 566 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 74 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
