/P 567 0 R
/E (Females are often preferred as candidates for parenting children, with biases being made known in many societal procedures \(e.g. courts, fostering, adoption\).)
/Pg 75 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
1847 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 567 0 R
/E (Research demonstrates empathy and parental care are major factors in childhood development \(Ainsworth et al, 1978\); however, the idea that maternal or paternal caretaking creating different systems of empathy in children is not strongly supported; rather it is found that the quality and responsiveness of parenting is most crucial in impacting offspring empathy development.)
/Pg 75 0 R
/K [13]
>>
