<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 568 0 R
/E (This conclusively demonstrates that, partially, empathy styles displayed in adulthood is determined biologically, as brain structures for empathy systems exist in infancy; with males being more likely to exhibit cognitive empathy, resorting to problem solving to display care, and females being prone to emotional empathy, displaying external emotive signals such as emotional contagion, empathy is largely learnt through parental responsiveness and quality.)
/Pg 76 0 R
/K [4]
>>
