/E (II. Failure of the project)
/Pg 84 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
2049 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 576 0 R
/E (Additionally, construction of the Troieshchyna part of the Podilsko-Vyhurivska metro line was delayed, with funding shortfalls a recurring problem on the project \(Kravets 2021\). The bridge contract has also been the subject of investigations: the Antimonopoly Committee fined the general contractor and another firm UAH 182.6 million for collusion in the 2017 tender, and prosecutors have alleged embezzlement \(Berezhanskyi 2025\). The delay and lack of funding likely worsened public transport problems, as residents of the left bank were left to commute by buses with uneven and sometimes delayed schedules. This probably led to the growth of the usage of private vehicles, which congested the streets even more, intensifying the transport crisis of Kyiv city.)
/Pg 84 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
2050 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 576 0 R
/E (One of the main reasons for the bridge construction delay, apart from financial issues, is the unreadiness of the construction ground \(Kravets 2021\). As the bridge is meant to connect Podil to the Dniprovskyi district, it is crossing a huge low-rise cottage residential area of Rusanivskyi Gardens \(Figure 3\), which has little infrastructure and housing. The problem, in fact, caused delays to the construction works while the area was prepared \(Kravets 2021\). Additionally, as the construction arose, major opposition was provoked among the residents of Rusanivskyi Gardens and ecologists who warned against the destruction of the Horbachykha natural tract \(Shnaider 2023\). Activists linked the protests to a failure of public consultation, as well as to the withdrawal of private land in Rusanivskyi Gardens \(Shnaider 2023; Kravets 2021\).)
/Pg 84 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
2051 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 576 0 R
/E (Another acute problem is the need for major construction works on the Paton Bridge, the South Bridge, and the Metro Bridge \(Kravets 2021\). Partial or complete blocking of these crossings might completely disrupt the flow of traffic, causing the transport collapse of the city. This could have been observed in the summer of 2022, when the South Bridge was closed to private vehicles \(Slovo i Dilo 2022\), leaving fewer crossings for traffic. Therefore, if these three major bridges are blocked, the finished parts of the Podilskyi Bridge are going to be exposed to a much higher amount of traffic, making completion much harder. )
/Pg 84 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
