/P 583 0 R
/E (This is exacerbated by their development stage, where teenagers actively seek community, approval and a sense of identity; therefore, they attach to the unverified diagnosis to fulfil their sense of belonging through identifying with a group with similar struggles10. )
/Pg 91 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
2157 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 583 0 R
/E (Whilst self-diagnosis can serve as a useful precursory acknowledgement, with research suggesting that individuals who believe they necessitated a clinical diagnosis often experience similar levels of severity \(psychopathology\) as those with clinical recognition of mental disorders10  \(suggesting better recognition of mental recognition\), professionals have expressed concern of misdiagnosis by adolescents . )
/Pg 91 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
2158 0 obj
<<
