/P 586 0 R
/E (Weitzman's intervention was the most productive move in the debate. But it shared with Stern and Nordhaus a premise so deeply embedded that none of them questioned it: that ecological damages are continuous and at least partially reversible through future wealth and technology. Studying both mathematics and biology has made one thing clear to me. This assumption is not merely optimistic. It is biologically false. )
/Pg 94 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
