/P 587 0 R
/E ( The second component is a near-zero rate for irreversible ecological harms. When no technological replacement exists for a functioning Amazon rainforest or a stable thermohaline circulation, the appropriate rate for those specific damages converges toward zero. The economics already supplies the mechanism. What it lacks is the institutional willingness to apply separate rates to separate categories of harm. )
/Pg 95 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
