<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 588 0 R
/E (A third objection holds that the framework is too complex to implement. But the UK already implements declining rates. France already implements declining rates. The question is not whether governments can manage variable discount structures \(they demonstrably can\) but whether those structures capture the distinct categories of environmental harm. I acknowledge a difficult operational question: where precisely should the boundary fall between the three categories? This is a limitation, but the difficulty of drawing boundaries does not invalidate the distinction. The difference between a reversible productivity loss and the irreversible collapse of the Atlantic thermohaline circulation is not a matter of degree. It is a difference in kind. )
/Pg 96 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
2236 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 588 0 R
/E ( Return to the opening calculation. At a declining rate starting at 3.5% and converging toward 1%, the present value of preventing planetary destruction two hundred years out is no longer 57 pence. It is orders of magnitude higher. Under the near-zero ecological rate, for damages that admit no substitution and no recovery, the present value approaches the undiscounted )
/Pg 96 0 R
/K [5]
>>
